          <p>
            The headline is that the cheapest concentrates, NOW and Nutricost, land around $1.50 to $1.60 per 25 g of protein, and the cheapest unflavored isolate we priced, NOW's own, is within a few cents of them. Within a single brand that sells both, the concentrate premium can be almost nothing. Across the market, though, the typical isolate still costs noticeably more: most flavored isolates we have priced elsewhere on the site fall between about $2 and $2.80 per 25 g, while flavored concentrates and concentrate-led blends cluster nearer $1.50 to $2.
